'============================================================
' Example 3: CR200X Variable Name Length Pitfalls
'
' On CR200(X) series dataloggers, Public variable names longer
' than 12 characters are truncated to 12 characters in output
' tables. Two variables that share the same first 12 characters
' then collide, producing a "duplicate field name" error at
' compile time on the real datalogger -- this extension predicts
' that error while you type.
'
' This file is deliberately imperfect: open it (as a .CR1 file,
' so the extension targets the CR200X model) to see the
' diagnostics described below.
'============================================================

Public RH ' fine: short name, no issue

' Warning only: 13 characters, over the 12-char recommendation,
' but under the 16-char hard limit.
Public Battery_Volt1

' Error + warning: 25 characters, over both the 12-char
' recommendation and the 16-char hard limit.
Public WindSpeedSensorNorthField

' Collision: both names share the first 12 characters
' ("Temperature_"), so both get truncated to the same output
' field name.
Public Temperature_S1
Public Temperature_S2

BeginProg
  Scan(5, Sec, 0, 0)
    Battery(Battery_Volt1)
  NextScan
EndProg
